course: dictionary
lesson: 14333
title: Obtuseness and the hint that never lands
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Obtuseness is a noun. It means being slow to understand, or not noticing what is obvious, even when the clues are right in front of you. «Tom's obtuseness made him miss every hint his sister dropped about the surprise party.» The hints were clear, but Tom did not get them, so obtuseness means slowness to understand.
explain: Stories often use this word for a character who will not take a hint. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad's friends despair at his obtuseness about his own foolishness: he cannot see how silly he has been, however plainly they point it out. Context tells you the feeling: the friends are frustrated, not pleased.
explain: The word has two other meanings you may meet. In maths, an obtuse angle is wider than a right angle, between 90° and 180°, so obtuseness is the quality of being that kind of angle. Also, obtuseness can mean bluntness, not being sharp or pointed: «The dull knife's obtuseness meant it could not cut the bread.» Check which meaning fits by swapping in your own meaning and reading the sentence again.
fact: Obtuseness is a noun, and it is usually uncountable: you say «his obtuseness», not «an obtuseness».
fact: Obtuseness means slowness to understand things, or not noticing what is obvious.
fact: In maths, an obtuse angle is between 90° and 180°, wider than a right angle.
fact: Obtuseness can also mean bluntness, not being sharp or pointed.
fact: Context clues help: if people are frustrated that someone will not get a hint, obtuseness means slowness to understand.
exercise: «Tom's obtuseness made him miss every hint his sister dropped about the surprise party.» What does obtuseness mean here? | Being kind to everyone at the party | Being very quick at sums | *Slowness to understand what is obvious
exercise: An angle of 120 degrees is wider than the corner of a square. Which word names this kind of angle? | Rightness | Curliness | Sharpness | *Obtuseness
exercise: «The blunt pencil's obtuseness made every line thick and fuzzy.» What does obtuseness mean here? | *Bluntness, not being sharp or pointed | Being very pointy | Being long and thin | Being very quick to draw
test: Which word is closest in meaning to obtuseness, meaning slowness to understand? | Speed | Brightness | *Dullness of understanding | Kindness
test: Toad's friends despaired at his obtuseness about his own foolishness. What were they finding hard? | Toad was too kind to blame anyone | Toad was too quick to notice his mistakes | *Toad would not see how foolish he had been, even when told | Toad was too sad to talk to them
exam: Which sentence uses obtuseness to mean bluntness? | *«The dull knife's obtuseness meant it could not cut the bread.» | «Her obtuseness was so clear that she solved the puzzle quickly.» | «Her obtuseness about the rain made her forget her coat.» | «The clever fox spotted the trap at once.»
